00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:45.000
and this is actually the fourth and the final part of our series

00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:49.000
titled Stranger Things When the Bible Gets Weird.

00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:53.000
And because next week is Advent, which is kind of hard to believe,

00:35:53.000 --> 00:35:57.000
but like it's the season of preparation for the birth of Christ.

00:35:57.000 --> 00:36:00.000
And it's always the Sunday after Thanksgiving,

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:02.000
which, by the way, Thanksgiving's coming up.

00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:05.000
So, you know, if you're not like on top of that, start thinking.

00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:08.000
You know, it's always these things always catch me off guard.

00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:10.000
Like, oh, my gosh, it's Thanksgiving.

00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:13.000
So that'll be into next Sunday.

00:36:13.000 --> 00:36:14.000
We'll get into Advent.

00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:16.000
So wrapping up the series tonight,

00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:22.000
and the title of the message is Mysterious Bodies.

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:24.000
Mysterious Bodies.

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:27.000
And the passage tonight is a little bit different.

00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:32.000
If you've been here for the series, you know, we've been looking at stories.

00:36:32.000 --> 00:36:37.000
Some of them, like some of them just have been a little bit strange or weird.

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:41.000
Something like Jonah and the Whale was one we looked at a few weeks back,

00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:45.000
where this prophet of God is swallowed by what the Bible calls a great fish.

00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:47.000
So we kind of unpack that story.

00:36:47.000 --> 00:36:50.000
And so sometimes it's stories like that where it's just sort of like strange.

00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:54.000
Others have been like sort of morally problematic,

00:36:54.000 --> 00:36:57.000
like the one we looked at last week, the story of the prophet Elisha

00:36:57.000 --> 00:37:01.000
and calling down a bear attack upon some youth.

00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:05.000
And so that's sort of, you know, weird and strange for a different reason.

00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:09.000
So I would say the one tonight, this might be kind of unique among them all.

00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:11.000
A, it's from the New Testament.

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:14.000
B, it's actually the words of Christ himself.

00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:20.000
And C, it's actually a verse that I quote, if not verbatim,

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:24.000
I at least allude to it every single week

00:37:24.000 --> 00:37:29.000
because it's part of our communion liturgy.

00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:34.000
And so because of that, you know, it's one of those passages

00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:37.000
that probably it just may not strike you as strange.

00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:40.000
And thus like, well, why is this in a series called Stranger Things?

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:41.000
This isn't weird.

00:37:41.000 --> 00:37:44.000
Although I want us to kind of read it again for the first time.

00:37:44.000 --> 00:37:47.000
You know, sometimes familiarity with a passage can just, I don't know,

00:37:47.000 --> 00:37:50.000
it's like the words are being said,

00:37:50.000 --> 00:37:56.000
but they're not hitting us as they might have, right, at first.

00:37:56.000 --> 00:37:59.000
And so let me go ahead and read it.

00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:03.000
This is from Matthew 26, verse 26, which says,

00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:06.000
While they were eating, Jesus took bread,

00:38:06.000 --> 00:38:09.000
and when he'd given thanks, he broke it,

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:12.000
and he gave it to his disciples, saying,

00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:20.000
Take and eat, this is my body.

00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:22.000
That's a strange phrase, isn't it?

00:38:22.000 --> 00:38:26.000
Like, this is my body, that's the key line for tonight.

00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:28.000
This is my body.

00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:30.000
I mean, is there, again, maybe you're so familiar with it,

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.000
you're just kind of like, oh yeah, of course, that's my body.

00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:38.000
But I'm guessing at some point maybe this struck you as a little strange.

00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:41.000
Maybe not, I don't know, maybe just quickly you're like,

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:44.000
well, he means it poetically, you know.

00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:48.000
But it's an interesting little turn of phrase.

00:38:48.000 --> 00:38:51.000
And I mean, I think at like a very literal level,

00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:54.000
like if I were not a Christian and hearing this for the first time,

00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:57.000
I think my first thought would honestly be just like,

00:38:57.000 --> 00:38:59.000
no, it's not.

00:38:59.000 --> 00:39:01.000
It's not your body, that's bread.

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:04.000
You're Jesus, and just not.

00:39:04.000 --> 00:39:07.000
I don't know, maybe you mean it in some other sense or something,

00:39:07.000 --> 00:39:10.000
but you're just, it's not, it's not your body.

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:13.000
It's bread, fat bread.

00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:16.000
So it is, it's a strange little turn of phrase.

00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:22.000
And I think the kind of question that I want driving the message tonight,

00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:26.000
and as I get into that I should name that I've been,

00:39:26.000 --> 00:39:28.000
last week I was drawing from Jonathan Paggio,

00:39:28.000 --> 00:39:30.000
Eastern Orthodox Christian thinker.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:33.000
This week it's from someone named Graham Ward

00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:36.000
in his book Cities of God, where he got me thinking about this passage

00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:38.000
in a new way, and thus I was like,

00:39:38.000 --> 00:39:41.000
oh, I must include this in the Stranger Things series.

00:39:41.000 --> 00:39:44.000
His book, oh, I said it, Cities of God.

00:39:44.000 --> 00:39:46.000
It's just wonderful.

00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:49.000
But he asks this question, which really caught me off guard.

00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:55.000
He said, well, what if Jesus is right?

00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:58.000
And it was strange, because I think probably it's my Protestantism.

00:39:58.000 --> 00:40:01.000
If you know, there's like a whole history and theological history

00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:03.000
to this statement, this is my body,

00:40:03.000 --> 00:40:06.000
and there's Protestants and Catholics and kind of diverge ways

00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:08.000
in interpreting this.

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:10.000
But it caught me off guard.

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:13.000
And kind of the thing I want to maybe push us to really consider

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:18.000
is like what if we think Jesus is wrong

00:40:18.000 --> 00:40:23.000
because we are making certain assumptions,

00:40:23.000 --> 00:40:28.000
certain kind of Western, some cultural assumptions

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:31.000
about what bodies are

00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:35.000
that we don't even realize we're making those assumptions.

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:36.000
Does that make sense?

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:39.000
It's sort of like the old saying about, you know,

00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:42.000
like one fish swimming by another fish,

00:40:42.000 --> 00:40:44.000
and the older fish says to the younger fish,

00:40:44.000 --> 00:40:46.000
hey, morning, how's the water?

00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:48.000
And then the younger fish says, what's water?

00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:53.000
And the idea being, right, a fish doesn't even know it's in water

00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:55.000
because that's called life.

00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:56.000
You know what I mean?

00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:59.000
In essence, it's so close to it, it's been there from the beginning

00:40:59.000 --> 00:41:02.000
that it's just, it's not even a thing.

00:41:02.000 --> 00:41:05.000
It's the thing that makes all other things possible.

00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:08.000
It's sort of like having a pair, another metaphor would be like lenses,

00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:11.000
like where you put on a pair of lenses and you're seen through the lenses.

00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:14.000
But if you had just worn glasses from the very beginning,

00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:16.000
you might forget, in fact, some of us do,

00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:18.000
like forget that we're even wearing glasses.

00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:20.000
In essence, you could think of that as like interpretations,

00:41:20.000 --> 00:41:23.000
cultural assumptions, or like lenses that we put on

00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:27.000
and we're seen through them, but we don't even realize we're doing it.

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:31.000
And I wonder if that's some of what's happening here.

00:41:31.000 --> 00:41:35.000
And it really centers around what bodies are.

00:41:35.000 --> 00:41:37.000
And by bodies, I mean this in a very diverse sense,

00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:41.000
like whether we're talking about the body of, say, like a rock,

00:41:41.000 --> 00:41:45.000
or the body of a flower, or the body of a piece of bread,

00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:48.000
or the body of a human being.

00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:52.000
For us, a body would be something like this,

00:41:52.000 --> 00:41:54.000
kind of as like a simplistic definition,

00:41:54.000 --> 00:41:59.000
like a body is like the visible structure of a thing.

00:41:59.000 --> 00:42:02.000
Right? It's kind of simple enough, straightforward.

00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:04.000
I'm like, yeah, that's what a body is.

00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:07.000
And kind of built into this assumption

00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:13.000
is that bodies are quite separate from one another.

00:42:13.000 --> 00:42:16.000
Right? Because if you have like a rock and a flower

00:42:16.000 --> 00:42:19.000
and a piece of bread and a human being,

00:42:19.000 --> 00:42:23.000
those bodies, those are, you know, separate bodies.

00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:25.000
To use kind of more academic language, you might say

00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:30.000
bodies are like autonomous, kind of self-defined,

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:33.000
self-enclosed things.

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:35.000
In other words, you know, like I'm over here

00:42:35.000 --> 00:42:40.000
and you all are over there, and we are separate bodies.

00:42:40.000 --> 00:42:43.000
Right? This is sort of how we tend to think of things.

00:42:43.000 --> 00:42:46.000
And inherent in that is that we don't think

00:42:46.000 --> 00:42:49.000
there's anything really connecting us.

00:42:49.000 --> 00:42:53.000
Right? Because of the separation, we are separate bodies.

00:42:53.000 --> 00:42:56.000
And, in fact, if we kind of start to say,

00:42:56.000 --> 00:43:01.000
well, actually, these bodies are more connected

00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:06.000
than you might realize, well, then we call that woo-woo.

00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:10.000
Right? We say, no, I don't really go in for woo-woo.

00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:15.000
I just, you know, I'm an American.

00:43:16.000 --> 00:43:20.000
It's obvious.

00:43:20.000 --> 00:43:23.000
But what's interesting is that's not really necessarily

00:43:23.000 --> 00:43:25.000
how the Bible seems to think of bodies,

00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:26.000
how specifically the New Testament,

00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:28.000
and really more specifically the Gospels,

00:43:28.000 --> 00:43:32.000
tends to think about bodies.

00:43:32.000 --> 00:43:35.000
And it doesn't seem to be what Jesus,

00:43:35.000 --> 00:43:37.000
how he seemed to think about bodies.

00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:41.000
And, you know, honestly, even, like I'm far from a, you know,

00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:43.000
scientist or quantum physicist or whatever,

00:43:43.000 --> 00:43:44.000
but just from the little I've picked up,

00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:46.000
even it seems like science, from what I can tell,

00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:49.000
is starting itself to get a little spooked.

00:43:49.000 --> 00:43:51.000
You know, even science is starting to sound a little woo-woo,

00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:52.000
you know, if you know anything about, like,

00:43:52.000 --> 00:43:54.000
quantum mechanics and such.

00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:59.000
Like, even everything out here that feels just so solid.

00:43:59.000 --> 00:44:02.000
You know, there's a body just, that's a body right there.

00:44:02.000 --> 00:44:03.000
You can't even hear it.

00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:04.000
That's what I'm talking about.

00:44:04.000 --> 00:44:05.000
That's not connected to anything.

00:44:05.000 --> 00:44:09.000
And yet, if you go down into, like, the subatomic level,

00:44:09.000 --> 00:44:14.000
it's actually mostly empty space and moving parts.

00:44:14.000 --> 00:44:15.000
And some scientists would even say

00:44:15.000 --> 00:44:18.000
it's maybe better described as, like, energy,

00:44:18.000 --> 00:44:20.000
which starts, you know, all of a sudden,

00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:21.000
your quantum, your physicist,

00:44:21.000 --> 00:44:23.000
like, starting to sound a little woo-woo, you know.

00:44:23.000 --> 00:44:24.000
It's like, okay.

00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:26.000
And then actually maybe some of those particles

00:44:26.000 --> 00:44:28.000
are somehow, like, connected to other things,

00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:30.000
such as they've done little experiments.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:31.000
You know, when you touch this one,

00:44:31.000 --> 00:44:32.000
like, you split the atom,

00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:33.000
and then you touch it over here,

00:44:33.000 --> 00:44:34.000
and this one's moving,

00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:35.000
even though they're supposed to be separate.

00:44:35.000 --> 00:44:36.000
But somehow they're not.

00:44:36.000 --> 00:44:38.000
And they're like, oh, gosh.

00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:39.000
Oh, gosh.

00:44:39.000 --> 00:44:40.000
We don't know how this is happening.

00:44:40.000 --> 00:44:41.000
Right?

00:44:41.000 --> 00:44:44.000
So it's getting a little spooked out there.

00:44:44.000 --> 00:44:48.000
But the point is that in the gospel specifically,

00:44:48.000 --> 00:44:52.000
bodies are not separate, self-defined,

00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:54.000
self-enclosed things.

00:44:54.000 --> 00:44:59.000
Instead, bodies constantly commune.

00:44:59.000 --> 00:45:01.000
Bodies pass through.

00:45:01.000 --> 00:45:03.000
Bodies share.

00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:07.000
And bodies can expand to include one another.

00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:11.000
In other words, bodies are much stranger,

00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:14.000
more wonderful, more mysterious things

00:45:14.000 --> 00:45:17.000
than we tend to imagine.

00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:19.000
And I think, you know, we might ask,

00:45:19.000 --> 00:45:21.000
well, how's that possible?

00:45:21.000 --> 00:45:27.000
I think it's because matter is not all that matters.

00:45:27.000 --> 00:45:31.000
In other words, matter is infused,

00:45:31.000 --> 00:45:35.000
enfolded, and upheld by God's spirit.

00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:37.000
In other words, everything that is,

00:45:37.000 --> 00:45:42.000
the visible world, things arise from God's spirit

00:45:42.000 --> 00:45:46.000
and in every moment are sustained by God's spirit

00:45:46.000 --> 00:45:50.000
such that a certain connection through God

00:45:50.000 --> 00:45:52.000
actually remains.

00:45:52.000 --> 00:45:54.000
This is what Gregory of Nyssa,

00:45:54.000 --> 00:45:56.000
the church father writing 1,500 years ago,

00:45:56.000 --> 00:46:00.000
he called it God's, all things are sustained,

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:04.000
upheld, enfolded by God's divine energy,

00:46:04.000 --> 00:46:06.000
which is sounding a little woo,

00:46:06.000 --> 00:46:08.000
but also like those, you know,

00:46:08.000 --> 00:46:10.000
some of those modern scientists

00:46:10.000 --> 00:46:13.000
where there's this energetic connection.

00:46:13.000 --> 00:46:16.000
Perhaps I might be losing you at this point.

00:46:16.000 --> 00:46:18.000
You're like, oh, this is all very deep.

00:46:18.000 --> 00:46:20.000
Let me give like a metaphor.

00:46:20.000 --> 00:46:22.000
There's a wonderful book called

00:46:22.000 --> 00:46:24.000
The Hidden Life of Trees.

00:46:24.000 --> 00:46:28.000
And Mindy earlier, my sister-in-law,

00:46:28.000 --> 00:46:32.000
she said this is such a Brett example.

00:46:32.000 --> 00:46:34.000
Like, who else would read this book?

00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:36.000
Like, well, it's so cool.

00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:39.000
I know, nerd, nerdy, nerdy.

00:46:39.000 --> 00:46:41.000
But in this book, it's really fascinating

00:46:41.000 --> 00:46:44.000
because, of course, when you look at trees,

00:46:44.000 --> 00:46:47.000
right, at the surface, the world of appearance,

00:46:47.000 --> 00:46:48.000
you know, what you can see,

00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:50.000
they just look so separate, don't they?

00:46:50.000 --> 00:46:54.000
Tree here, tree there, tree there, tree there.

00:46:54.000 --> 00:46:57.000
And maybe another leaf's touch or something, you know.

00:46:57.000 --> 00:46:59.000
But outside of that, like, they're separate.

00:46:59.000 --> 00:47:01.000
But what are ecologists learning

00:47:01.000 --> 00:47:05.000
that actually beneath the surface,

00:47:05.000 --> 00:47:09.000
their roots are intertwining

00:47:09.000 --> 00:47:13.000
and they are communicating

00:47:13.000 --> 00:47:17.000
and they are even co-sharing?

00:47:17.000 --> 00:47:18.000
Do you know this?

00:47:18.000 --> 00:47:23.000
Trees share nutrients with one another.

00:47:23.000 --> 00:47:24.000
Like, if this one's in need,

00:47:24.000 --> 00:47:27.000
it can like send nutrients.

00:47:27.000 --> 00:47:30.000
Like, what?

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:33.000
They are co-evolving.

00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:37.000
They are co-growing.

00:47:37.000 --> 00:47:39.000
And so while on the surface, right,

00:47:39.000 --> 00:47:41.000
it looks like, what, separate trees.

00:47:41.000 --> 00:47:42.000
That's how bodies are.

00:47:42.000 --> 00:47:45.000
They're all just separate things, you know.

00:47:45.000 --> 00:47:47.000
But I think this is a perfect picture

00:47:47.000 --> 00:47:51.000
of really what kind of the New Testament's hinting at

00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:53.000
about not just, you know, trees,

00:47:53.000 --> 00:47:55.000
but really all bodies,

00:47:55.000 --> 00:47:57.000
that beneath what we can see,

00:47:57.000 --> 00:48:00.000
there is a connection, right?

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:02.000
So while we think you got a person here

00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:03.000
and a person there

00:48:03.000 --> 00:48:04.000
and a dog over there

00:48:04.000 --> 00:48:06.000
and a flower over here

00:48:06.000 --> 00:48:07.000
and they look so separate,

00:48:07.000 --> 00:48:09.000
but at the unseen level,

00:48:09.000 --> 00:48:12.000
the level of spirit,

00:48:12.000 --> 00:48:14.000
there's a profound connection.

00:48:14.000 --> 00:48:15.000
And why is that?

00:48:15.000 --> 00:48:17.000
Again, because the material world

00:48:17.000 --> 00:48:20.000
arises from the spiritual world.

00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:23.000
And so there, a connection remains.

00:48:23.000 --> 00:48:25.000
Another example that would be

00:48:25.000 --> 00:48:27.000
more human-like is,

00:48:27.000 --> 00:48:28.000
did you all know,

00:48:28.000 --> 00:48:30.000
so here you are all sitting,

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.000
and unless you have your significant other,

00:48:32.000 --> 00:48:33.000
you're probably not touching.

00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:34.000
That would be a little strange,

00:48:34.000 --> 00:48:37.000
like someone just randomly like, hey.

00:48:37.000 --> 00:48:38.000
And yet, did you know,

00:48:38.000 --> 00:48:39.000
even as you all sit there

00:48:39.000 --> 00:48:41.000
looking like such separate bodies,

00:48:41.000 --> 00:48:43.000
did you know that this whole time

00:48:43.000 --> 00:48:46.000
your bodies have been tuning into one another?

00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:48.000
Like you have, for example,

00:48:48.000 --> 00:48:52.000
pheromones have been passing.

00:48:52.000 --> 00:48:55.000
And even there's something called limbic resonance,

00:48:55.000 --> 00:48:56.000
which is a really weird idea.

00:48:56.000 --> 00:48:58.000
It's basically this idea that

00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:01.000
your brain tunes into,

00:49:01.000 --> 00:49:07.000
picks up on the kind of mind attunement of others,

00:49:07.000 --> 00:49:11.000
the moods, the emotional kind of tenor

00:49:11.000 --> 00:49:14.000
of other minds,

00:49:14.000 --> 00:49:18.000
and you attune yourself to them.

00:49:18.000 --> 00:49:20.000
You sync up with them.

00:49:21.000 --> 00:49:22.000
This is why, for example,

00:49:22.000 --> 00:49:24.000
you might walk through those doors

00:49:24.000 --> 00:49:27.000
and feel massively depressed.

00:49:27.000 --> 00:49:29.000
And then ever so subtly,

00:49:29.000 --> 00:49:30.000
you come here,

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:34.000
and even if you never say a word to anyone,

00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:37.000
you just start feeling better.

00:49:37.000 --> 00:49:39.000
What's happening there?

00:49:39.000 --> 00:49:42.000
Your bodies are amazing.

00:49:42.000 --> 00:49:44.000
Your bodies are more than you think.

00:49:44.000 --> 00:49:45.000
You don't walk in these doors,

00:49:45.000 --> 00:49:46.000
and you're not just some autonomous,

00:49:46.000 --> 00:49:48.000
self-defined, self-enclosed thing

00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:50.000
choosing occasionally to speak a word and connect.

00:49:50.000 --> 00:49:52.000
No, no, no.

00:49:52.000 --> 00:49:54.000
Your bodies are always already

00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:58.000
tuning in to one another.

00:49:58.000 --> 00:50:02.000
So, let's go ahead and return to Christ.

00:50:02.000 --> 00:50:03.000
And let's talk about His body.

00:50:03.000 --> 00:50:04.000
We could talk about all sorts of things.

00:50:04.000 --> 00:50:06.000
We could talk about the miracles He did

00:50:06.000 --> 00:50:07.000
with His body, right?

00:50:07.000 --> 00:50:09.000
And with bodies,

00:50:09.000 --> 00:50:11.000
things with multiplying the body of bread

00:50:11.000 --> 00:50:15.000
and feeding people or healing human bodies and such.

00:50:15.000 --> 00:50:17.000
We could talk about the fascinating nature

00:50:17.000 --> 00:50:18.000
of His resurrected body.

00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:20.000
He could pass through walls

00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:22.000
or appear to people such that they

00:50:22.000 --> 00:50:23.000
at first couldn't recognize Him,

00:50:23.000 --> 00:50:25.000
but then suddenly they could recognize Him.

00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:27.000
And there's all sorts of weird, mysterious things

00:50:27.000 --> 00:50:30.000
about Christ's resurrected body.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:31.000
All sorts of things.

00:50:31.000 --> 00:50:32.000
But above all,

00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:33.000
what I want to focus in on

00:50:33.000 --> 00:50:36.000
is the capacity of Christ's body

00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:42.000
to expand and to include other bodies.

00:50:42.000 --> 00:50:43.000
I think above all things,

00:50:43.000 --> 00:50:47.000
this is like the strangest, most wonderful idea.

00:50:47.000 --> 00:50:50.000
Now, key to this is what's known as the ascension.

00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:52.000
And Graham Ward points out,

00:50:52.000 --> 00:50:53.000
after the resurrection,

00:50:53.000 --> 00:50:55.000
you have the ascension of Jesus.

00:50:55.000 --> 00:51:00.000
And this isn't about Jesus disappearing.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:03.000
Like it's like, oh no, Jesus, you're gone.

00:51:03.000 --> 00:51:06.000
Instead, Christ ascends

00:51:06.000 --> 00:51:12.000
so that His body can begin to fill all things.

00:51:12.000 --> 00:51:14.000
And this becomes really key.

00:51:14.000 --> 00:51:18.000
So He ascends so that His body can expand

00:51:18.000 --> 00:51:21.000
and He can make good on His promise in Matthew 18-20.

00:51:21.000 --> 00:51:22.000
Maybe you've read this passage

00:51:22.000 --> 00:51:24.000
and it has never made sense to you,

00:51:24.000 --> 00:51:26.000
but it says this,

00:51:26.000 --> 00:51:29.000
For where two or three gather in My name,

00:51:29.000 --> 00:51:34.000
there am I with them.

00:51:34.000 --> 00:51:38.000
This is about the expansion of Christ's body.

00:51:38.000 --> 00:51:40.000
And again, at one level, we might think,

00:51:40.000 --> 00:51:42.000
what, no, that's impossible.

00:51:42.000 --> 00:51:44.000
This isn't how bodies work.

00:51:44.000 --> 00:51:46.000
But what if we're wrong?

00:51:46.000 --> 00:51:48.000
And what if Jesus is right?

00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:51.000
He ascends and His body expands

00:51:51.000 --> 00:51:53.000
so that He can, coming back to our original text,

00:51:53.000 --> 00:51:56.000
Matthew 26-26, make good on His promise.

00:51:56.000 --> 00:52:01.000
Take and eat, this is My body.

00:52:01.000 --> 00:52:04.000
He ascends so that,

00:52:04.000 --> 00:52:07.000
as Ephesians 1-22-23 names,

00:52:07.000 --> 00:52:10.000
Christ's body can envelop the body of the church

00:52:10.000 --> 00:52:14.000
such that we call the church the what of Christ?

00:52:14.000 --> 00:52:18.000
The body of Christ.

00:52:18.000 --> 00:52:19.000
I mean, this is,

00:52:19.000 --> 00:52:20.000
think of that,

00:52:20.000 --> 00:52:22.000
Christ's body has now expanded

00:52:22.000 --> 00:52:26.000
to include each and every one of you.

00:52:26.000 --> 00:52:30.000
This, like, this is a fascinating,

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:35.000
strange, beautiful idea.

00:52:36.000 --> 00:52:38.000
Okay, so that's a lot of theology.

00:52:38.000 --> 00:52:39.000
I want to kind of bring this back to, like,

00:52:39.000 --> 00:52:43.000
okay, so what does this actually mean for our lives?

00:52:43.000 --> 00:52:45.000
Let me give you four takeaways.

00:52:45.000 --> 00:52:48.000
First, My body, your body,

00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:51.000
is more mysterious and wonderful

00:52:51.000 --> 00:52:54.000
than you or I have ever dreamed.

00:52:54.000 --> 00:52:56.000
In other words, you are not just cells

00:52:56.000 --> 00:52:59.000
and atoms and, like, dead matter.

00:52:59.000 --> 00:53:03.000
You are a beautiful, wonderful living body

00:53:03.000 --> 00:53:06.000
shot through with God's Spirit,

00:53:06.000 --> 00:53:10.000
with more ability to be influenced by other bodies,

00:53:10.000 --> 00:53:12.000
all bodies, again, not just human beings,

00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:16.000
trees and flowers and rocks and all of it,

00:53:16.000 --> 00:53:19.000
and with more capacity to influence others' bodies

00:53:19.000 --> 00:53:20.000
than you might dream,

00:53:20.000 --> 00:53:23.000
which leads to our second insight or takeaway.

00:53:23.000 --> 00:53:26.000
I am both influencing others' bodies

00:53:26.000 --> 00:53:29.000
and being influenced by them, by their bodies,

00:53:29.000 --> 00:53:32.000
far more than I am aware of.

00:53:32.000 --> 00:53:36.000
I think of the strange thing human beings do

00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:41.000
where we go to coffee shops to work or study or read

00:53:41.000 --> 00:53:44.000
to be alone with other people.

00:53:44.000 --> 00:53:46.000
Isn't that a strange thing?

00:53:46.000 --> 00:53:48.000
It's like, well, I could just be alone at my house,

00:53:48.000 --> 00:53:51.000
but I'd rather be alone with other people.

00:53:51.000 --> 00:53:53.000
Why?

00:53:53.000 --> 00:53:55.000
It's all this we're talking about.

00:53:55.000 --> 00:53:57.000
Like, there's just something about

00:53:57.000 --> 00:54:00.000
being with other human bodies

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:03.000
and it just impacts us

00:54:03.000 --> 00:54:06.000
in ways that we usually like.

00:54:06.000 --> 00:54:07.000
This is also why, of course,

00:54:07.000 --> 00:54:09.000
like concerts and places where you get

00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:11.000
like tens of thousands of bodies all together,

00:54:11.000 --> 00:54:14.000
it's just crazy what can kind of happen

00:54:14.000 --> 00:54:17.000
because there's something really almost magical

00:54:17.000 --> 00:54:20.000
about human bodies.

00:54:20.000 --> 00:54:24.000
Third, I am affected even by those bodies

00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:28.000
whom I claim to exclude.

00:54:28.000 --> 00:54:30.000
This is an interesting insight from Graham Ward.

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:31.000
He writes this.

00:54:31.000 --> 00:54:34.000
He says, that which I exclude from my body

00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:37.000
or that which is excluded in my name

00:54:37.000 --> 00:54:40.000
from the institutions, social circles, and such

00:54:40.000 --> 00:54:41.000
to which I belong,

00:54:41.000 --> 00:54:45.000
will affect me for good or for ill.

00:54:45.000 --> 00:54:48.000
The ghettoizations and the segregation of,

00:54:48.000 --> 00:54:49.000
and he lists all the isms,

00:54:49.000 --> 00:54:53.000
racism or sexism or classism or ageism,

00:54:53.000 --> 00:54:57.000
done in my name or condoned by my silence

00:54:57.000 --> 00:54:59.000
injure me.

00:54:59.000 --> 00:55:00.000
Notice Ward doesn't say there,

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.000
it injures them, those excluded.

00:55:02.000 --> 00:55:03.000
Though, of course, that's like so obvious

00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:05.000
he didn't feel the need to name it.

00:55:05.000 --> 00:55:06.000
But the interesting insight is

00:55:06.000 --> 00:55:10.000
that actually injures me.

00:55:10.000 --> 00:55:13.000
But why on earth is this?

00:55:13.000 --> 00:55:17.000
Because those, when I unjustly exclude someone,

00:55:17.000 --> 00:55:20.000
I think that I'm cutting them off, right?

00:55:20.000 --> 00:55:24.000
My body no longer has anything to do with their body.

00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:28.000
But because of the mysterious, magical nature of bodies,

00:55:28.000 --> 00:55:31.000
actually a connection remains.

00:55:31.000 --> 00:55:35.000
No matter how kind of distorted

00:55:35.000 --> 00:55:42.000
or marred that connection is.

00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:44.000
In fact, I think our last series we did, Unclean,

00:55:44.000 --> 00:55:47.000
I think is really deepened by all of this insight

00:55:47.000 --> 00:55:52.000
about bodies and the nature of what bodies actually are.

00:55:52.000 --> 00:55:53.000
Fourth and finally,

00:55:53.000 --> 00:55:57.000
growing in Christ is an act of expansion.

00:55:57.000 --> 00:56:02.000
Expanding my body to include, love, relate to,

00:56:02.000 --> 00:56:06.000
and commune with all other bodies.

00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:10.000
Again, Gregory of Nyssa, writing many moons ago,

00:56:10.000 --> 00:56:11.000
he says,

00:56:11.000 --> 00:56:13.000
Participation in the divine good is such that

00:56:13.000 --> 00:56:15.000
where it occurs, it makes the participant

00:56:15.000 --> 00:56:19.000
ever greater and more spacious than before.

00:56:19.000 --> 00:56:21.000
Brings to it, that would be you and I,

00:56:21.000 --> 00:56:25.000
an increase in size and strength in such wise

00:56:25.000 --> 00:56:27.000
that the participant nourished in this way

00:56:27.000 --> 00:56:32.000
never stops growing and keeps getting larger and larger.

00:56:32.000 --> 00:56:35.000
He's not talking about body building.

00:56:35.000 --> 00:56:37.000
Instead, he's talking,

00:56:37.000 --> 00:56:40.000
well, he's saying one way to think of your life in Christ

00:56:40.000 --> 00:56:42.000
and of your wonderful body

00:56:42.000 --> 00:56:46.000
is that it is always either expanding

00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:50.000
or it is shrinking.

00:56:50.000 --> 00:56:52.000
And I think of, in other words,

00:56:52.000 --> 00:56:57.000
our bodies are either becoming more spacious,

00:56:57.000 --> 00:56:59.000
growing, expanding,

00:56:59.000 --> 00:57:02.000
to include everything and everyone

00:57:02.000 --> 00:57:07.000
from people to trees to rocks to flowers to human beings,

00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:11.000
or we are shrinking down.

00:57:11.000 --> 00:57:14.000
I think, for example, of like an addict

00:57:14.000 --> 00:57:17.000
and what's happened with an addict.

00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:21.000
Their whole world has shrunk down to their body

00:57:21.000 --> 00:57:24.000
and the body of their drug.

00:57:24.000 --> 00:57:28.000
And that's like the limit of their world.

00:57:28.000 --> 00:57:32.000
They are a shrinking self.

00:57:32.000 --> 00:57:34.000
But on the opposite end of that spectrum

00:57:34.000 --> 00:57:38.000
is like kind of someone like the spiritual person

00:57:38.000 --> 00:57:42.000
or a follower of Christ who's journeyed far in that.

00:57:42.000 --> 00:57:43.000
What happens?

00:57:43.000 --> 00:57:50.000
Our body grows and expands to include all things.

00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:53.000
I think of, for example, I'll close with this.

00:57:53.000 --> 00:57:56.000
Some of us went to the Sinner Peace Conference

00:57:56.000 --> 00:57:58.000
a few weeks back.

00:57:58.000 --> 00:58:00.000
And Sinner Peace is an organization

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.000
that's helping the church have better conversations

00:58:02.000 --> 00:58:06.000
around theology and sexuality and sexual orientation.

00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:11.000
And it's run by a wonderful woman named Sally Gary.

00:58:11.000 --> 00:58:16.000
And if you've ever met Sally, she is just great.

00:58:16.000 --> 00:58:18.000
She's kind of that perfect, wonderful mixture

00:58:18.000 --> 00:58:25.000
of kind but confident,

00:58:25.000 --> 00:58:30.000
humble, loving, wise.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:32.000
She's just the person.

00:58:32.000 --> 00:58:35.000
You get around her and she's got that good energy.

00:58:35.000 --> 00:58:36.000
You know what I mean?

00:58:36.000 --> 00:58:37.000
You like her.

00:58:37.000 --> 00:58:43.000
And what I noticed is that just like Christ's body

00:58:43.000 --> 00:58:46.000
has sort of expanded or is in the process of expanding

00:58:46.000 --> 00:58:48.000
to include all things,

00:58:48.000 --> 00:58:55.000
that anyone who goes to that conference

00:58:55.000 --> 00:59:01.000
in a sense has communed with the body of Sally Gary

00:59:01.000 --> 00:59:05.000
even if you never spoke to her.

00:59:06.000 --> 00:59:08.000
Again, call it the woo-woo word that you want.

00:59:08.000 --> 00:59:13.000
Her essence, her energy, her body

00:59:13.000 --> 00:59:17.000
has so saturated that community

00:59:17.000 --> 00:59:19.000
that it's like, I don't know,

00:59:19.000 --> 00:59:20.000
it's like everywhere you go,

00:59:20.000 --> 00:59:24.000
people have just taken on the spirit of Sally Gary.

00:59:24.000 --> 00:59:26.000
And suddenly that whole community

00:59:26.000 --> 00:59:30.000
is more than it would have been otherwise.

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:33.000
More spacious, more patient,

00:59:33.000 --> 00:59:36.000
more loving, more kind, more humble.

00:59:36.000 --> 00:59:37.000
What's happened?

00:59:37.000 --> 00:59:41.000
Just like Christ, Sally Gary has expanded

00:59:41.000 --> 00:59:45.000
and filled a community.

00:59:45.000 --> 00:59:49.000
And I think the same is true for each and every one of us

00:59:49.000 --> 00:59:51.000
or can be true,

00:59:51.000 --> 00:59:55.000
that you and I are more than just cells

00:59:55.000 --> 00:59:58.000
but instead we are called to grow,

00:59:59.000 --> 01:00:04.000
to expand, to make room for people.

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:09.000
And so my prayer is that may your body become large

01:00:09.000 --> 01:00:14.000
and like Christ fill all things and all people.

01:00:14.000 --> 01:00:18.000
So as we come to the table of the Lord tonight,

01:00:18.000 --> 01:00:26.000
I hope that it takes on just a bit more of a rich meaning

01:00:26.000 --> 01:00:29.000
where instead of being only a metaphor

01:00:29.000 --> 01:00:32.000
or only a symbol,

01:00:32.000 --> 01:00:34.000
it becomes more than that.

01:00:34.000 --> 01:00:36.000
Where we actually start to trust

01:00:36.000 --> 01:00:40.000
that Christ's body is present to us

01:00:40.000 --> 01:00:43.000
in bread and in wine.

01:00:43.000 --> 01:00:48.000
And that as we take in Christ and consume him,

01:00:48.000 --> 01:00:53.000
that somehow he's taking us in.

01:00:53.000 --> 01:00:58.000
And maybe even in a good way kind of breaking us open

01:00:58.000 --> 01:01:03.000
and then giving us to a very, very needy world.

01:01:03.000 --> 01:01:06.000
So we practice here at the table what's called an open table.

01:01:06.000 --> 01:01:09.000
Meaning if you're here tonight and you want to participate,

01:01:09.000 --> 01:01:12.000
then you are free to do that.

01:01:12.000 --> 01:01:13.000
And the way we'll come forward

01:01:13.000 --> 01:01:15.000
is we'll start with these kind of front rows

01:01:15.000 --> 01:01:16.000
and we'll just work our way back

01:01:16.000 --> 01:01:18.000
so we don't get a super long line.

01:01:18.000 --> 01:01:21.000
And then finally you're just free to partake of the elements

01:01:21.000 --> 01:01:23.000
whenever you'd like, whether it's immediately

01:01:23.000 --> 01:01:26.000
or you can go back to your chair and sit down.

01:01:26.000 --> 01:01:27.000
So let me invite you to the table.

01:01:27.000 --> 01:01:29.000
This is a Celtic Christian invitation.

01:01:29.000 --> 01:01:34.000
This is the table, not of the church, but of the Lord.

01:01:34.000 --> 01:01:36.000
And it's made ready for those who love him

01:01:36.000 --> 01:01:38.000
and for those who want to love him more.

01:01:38.000 --> 01:01:40.000
So come.

01:01:40.000 --> 01:01:43.000
You who have much faith and you who have little.

01:01:43.000 --> 01:01:45.000
You who have been here often

01:01:45.000 --> 01:01:47.000
and you who have not been here long.

01:01:47.000 --> 01:01:51.000
You who have tried to follow and you who have failed.

01:01:51.000 --> 01:01:53.000
Come.

01:01:53.000 --> 01:01:56.000
Because it's the Lord himself who invites you.

01:01:56.000 --> 01:01:59.000
And it's his will that those who want to meet him

01:01:59.000 --> 01:02:01.000
should meet him here.

01:02:01.000 --> 01:02:03.000
Come to the table.

01:02:17.000 --> 01:02:19.000
Come to the table.

01:02:47.000 --> 01:02:49.000
Come to the table.

01:03:17.000 --> 01:03:19.000
Come to the table.

01:03:47.000 --> 01:03:49.000
Come.

01:04:17.000 --> 01:04:19.000
Come.

01:04:47.000 --> 01:04:49.000
Come.

01:05:18.000 --> 01:05:22.000
I love what, um, Karin said.

01:05:22.000 --> 01:05:24.000
As we were starting our service,

01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:26.000
she referred to something, um,

01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:29.000
said something to the effect of,

01:05:29.000 --> 01:05:33.000
we're not really free until all of us are free.

01:05:33.000 --> 01:05:37.000
And, um, that has stuck with me all week.

01:05:37.000 --> 01:05:39.000
We had a call earlier in the week

01:05:39.000 --> 01:05:41.000
when we were planning out this service

01:05:41.000 --> 01:05:44.000
and talking about Trans Remembrance Day,

01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:46.000
and, um, and she said that phrase.

01:05:46.000 --> 01:05:49.000
And it just has been going through my head

01:05:49.000 --> 01:05:51.000
as I practiced the worship set,

01:05:51.000 --> 01:05:53.000
as I was thinking about being together today

01:05:53.000 --> 01:05:56.000
with all of you, and, um,

01:05:56.000 --> 01:06:00.000
just how strangely interconnected

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:03.000
I have come to feel with this community.

01:06:03.000 --> 01:06:06.000
And just, um,

01:06:06.000 --> 01:06:08.000
you know, I carry you guys in my heart.

01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:13.000
And, um, knowing that

01:06:13.000 --> 01:06:16.000
when tragedies happen, um,

01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:18.000
in our community or outside of our community

01:06:18.000 --> 01:06:20.000
and people are impacted by it,

01:06:20.000 --> 01:06:22.000
we carry you guys with us.

01:06:22.000 --> 01:06:26.000
You know, you're like this unseen member,

01:06:26.000 --> 01:06:29.000
um, in my life as I go throughout my day

01:06:29.000 --> 01:06:31.000
or as I plan a worship set

01:06:31.000 --> 01:06:33.000
or, you know, whatever's going on.

01:06:33.000 --> 01:06:36.000
And, um, we were trying to think of a song

01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:38.000
to finish with tonight.

01:06:38.000 --> 01:06:41.000
And this song that, we've done it once before

01:06:41.000 --> 01:06:44.000
when we talked about some racial equality

01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:49.000
and, um, and the words just seem so fitting.

01:06:49.000 --> 01:06:53.000
Um, any time that we're facing a situation

01:06:53.000 --> 01:06:56.000
where there's a group of people

01:06:56.000 --> 01:07:01.000
who are not experiencing the freedom that they should,

01:07:01.000 --> 01:07:03.000
this song comes to mind.

01:07:03.000 --> 01:07:05.000
And as we sing it today, um,

01:07:05.000 --> 01:07:07.000
I just hope that, like, in my head,

01:07:07.000 --> 01:07:10.000
I see us like there are no aisles, you know,

01:07:10.000 --> 01:07:13.000
we're all like kumbayaing together.

01:07:13.000 --> 01:07:15.000
There are lights, like a concert.

01:07:15.000 --> 01:07:16.000
You know what I mean?

01:07:16.000 --> 01:07:17.000
This is like, in my head,

01:07:17.000 --> 01:07:22.000
this is this moment of, like, unity and togetherness

01:07:22.000 --> 01:07:24.000
where we're holding up each other's arms.

01:07:24.000 --> 01:07:25.000
You know what I mean?

01:07:25.000 --> 01:07:27.000
Because some of us are feeling heavier than others.

01:07:27.000 --> 01:07:29.000
Some of us are feeling the effects

01:07:29.000 --> 01:07:31.000
of what's going on more than the rest.

01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:34.000
But together, we're able to hold up each other's arms,

01:07:34.000 --> 01:07:37.000
feel it together, carry the weight together,

01:07:37.000 --> 01:07:39.000
shoulder our burdens together.

01:07:39.000 --> 01:07:42.000
And that's the beauty of the body of Christ.

01:07:42.000 --> 01:07:45.000
Um, it is that interconnectedness.

01:07:45.000 --> 01:07:49.000
So know that as we finish this time together

01:07:49.000 --> 01:07:52.000
that you guys are, um, prayed for,

01:07:52.000 --> 01:07:55.000
that you're loved, that you're remembered.

01:07:55.000 --> 01:07:58.000
Um, so would you guys just stand with us?

01:07:58.000 --> 01:08:01.000
And even if this is a song that you're unfamiliar with,

01:08:01.000 --> 01:08:04.000
I just, I want us to stand in that posture

01:08:04.000 --> 01:08:07.000
of, um, being there for one another,

01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:10.000
um, carrying one another's burdens

01:08:10.000 --> 01:08:13.000
and believing for a future hope,

01:08:13.000 --> 01:08:17.000
for that prophetic creativity that Karen referred to earlier,

01:08:17.000 --> 01:08:22.000
that there will be a day where every tear is dried,

01:08:22.000 --> 01:08:24.000
where all the sins are washed away,

01:08:24.000 --> 01:08:28.000
and we are walking in the freedom of Christ together.

